#: THEORY.md:1
msgid "PLUMED Masterclass 21.4: Metadynamics"
msgstr "PLUMED Masterclass 21.4：Metadynamics"

#: THEORY.md:3
msgid "Background theory"
msgstr "背景理論"

#: THEORY.md:5
msgid ""
"In [metadynamics](https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.202427399), an "
"external history-dependent bias potential is constructed in the space of a "
"few selected degrees of freedom $\\vec{s}({q})$, generally called collective"
" variables (CVs). This potential is built as a sum of Gaussian kernels "
"deposited along the trajectory in the CVs space:"
msgstr ""
"[Metadynamics](https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.202427399) は、Collective"
" Variables (CVs) と呼ぶ少数の自由度 $\\vec{s}({q})$ の空間に、外部の履歴依存 BiasPotential "
"を構築します。CV 空間の Trajectory に沿って Gaussian Kernel を足し合わせます。"

#: THEORY.md:14
msgid ""
"where $\\tau$ is the Gaussian deposition stride, $\\sigma_i$ the width of "
"the Gaussian for the $i$th CV, and $W(k \\tau)$ is the height of the "
"Gaussian. The effect of the metadynamics bias potential is to push the "
"system away from local minima into visiting new regions of the phase space. "
"Furthermore, in the long time limit, the bias potential converges to minus "
"the free energy as a function of the CVs:"
msgstr ""
"$\\tau$ は Gaussian 追加の Stride、$\\sigma_i$ は $i$ 番目の CV の Gaussian 幅、$W(k "
"\\tau)$ は高さです。BiasPotential は系を局所極小から押し出し、新しい Phase Space を訪れさせます。長時間極限では、CV"
" の関数としての自由エネルギーの符号反転に収束します。"

#: THEORY.md:20
msgid ""
"In standard metadynamics, Gaussian kernels of constant height are added for "
"the entire course of a simulation. As a result, the system is eventually "
"pushed to explore high free-energy regions and the estimate of the free "
"energy calculated from the bias potential oscillates around the real value. "
"In [well-tempered "
"metadynamics](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.100.020603),"
" the height of the Gaussian is decreased with simulation time according to:"
msgstr ""
"標準 Metadynamics では高さ一定の Gaussian "
"を全期間追加するため、最終的には高自由エネルギー領域まで探索し、BiasPotential からの推定は真値の周囲で振動します。[Well-"
"tempered "
"Metadynamics](https://journals.aps.org/prl/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevLett.100.020603)"
" は、時間とともに高さを次のように減らします。"

#: THEORY.md:26
msgid ""
"where $W_0$ is an initial Gaussian height, $\\Delta T$ an input parameter "
"with the dimension of a temperature, and $k_B$ is the Boltzmann constant. "
"With this rescaling of the Gaussian height, the bias potential smoothly "
"converges in the long time limit, but it does not fully compensate the "
"underlying free energy:"
msgstr ""
"$W_0$ は初期 Gaussian 高さ、$\\Delta T$ は温度の次元を持つ入力パラメータ、$k_B$ は Boltzmann "
"定数です。高さの Rescaling により長時間極限で滑らかに収束しますが、自由エネルギーを完全には打ち消しません。"

#: THEORY.md:32
msgid ""
"where $T$ is the temperature of the system. In the long time limit, the CVs "
"thus sample an ensemble at a temperature $T+\\Delta T$ which is higher than "
"the system temperature $T$. The parameter $\\Delta T$ can be chosen to "
"regulate the extent of free-energy exploration: $\\Delta T = 0$ corresponds "
"to standard MD, $\\Delta T \\rightarrow\\infty$ to standard metadynamics. In"
" well-tempered metadynamics literature and in PLUMED, you will often "
"encounter the term \"bias factor\" which is the ratio between the "
"temperature of the CVs ($ T+\\Delta T$) and the system temperature ($T$):"
msgstr ""
"$T$ は系の温度です。長時間極限で CV は、系の温度 $T$ より高い $T+\\Delta T$ の Ensemble を Sampling "
"します。$\\Delta T$ で自由エネルギー探索の範囲を調整でき、$\\Delta T = 0$ は標準 MD、$\\Delta T "
"\\rightarrow\\infty$ は標準 Metadynamics です。文献や PLUMED の「Bias Factor」は、CV 温度（$ "
"T+\\Delta T$）と系の温度（$T$）の比です。"

#: THEORY.md:38
msgid ""
"The bias factor should thus be carefully chosen in order for the relevant "
"free-energy barriers to be crossed efficiently in the time scale of the "
"simulation."
msgstr "重要な自由エネルギー Barrier をシミュレーション時間内に効率よく越えられるよう、Bias Factor を慎重に選びます。"
